\begin{theorem}[Euler number of a Kuhn cusp]\label{maps:src:F.1.1}
\StatementRecord{maps:src:F.1.1}{proved}{GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, 2026-11-17; GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), S6\_06\_BLIND, effort Pro, 2026-11-17; Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic), effort high, 16 November 2026; also checked in this writing by \CurrentChecker}{the hypotheses, notation and definitions stated here; the explicit constructions and calculations in the proof}


Let $g:M^8\to S^2$ be a proper triangulable map, a $T^6$-bundle
off finitely many values.  Suppose its unique non-quotient special
fibre is the rank-three Kuhn toroidal fibre with period-lattice
index $d$, and all its other special reduced fibres are free
finite quotients of $T^6$.  Then $\chi(M)=6d$.

\end{theorem}

\begin{proposition}[the diagonal obstruction]\label{maps:src:F.1.4}
\StatementRecord{maps:src:F.1.4}{proved}{GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), effort Pro, 2026-11-17; Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic), effort high, 16 November 2026; also checked in this writing by \CurrentChecker}{the hypotheses, notation and definitions stated here; the explicit constructions and calculations in the proof}


If $A\in\operatorname{GL}_n(\mathbb Z)$ has no eigenvalue one,
every affine map $x\mapsto Ax+b$ of $\mathbb R^n/\mathbb Z^n$
has a fixed point.  Thus the diagonal elliptic finite monodromies
in Lead 7 admit no free affine lifts.

\end{proposition}

\begin{proposition}[a complete finite-order filter]\label{maps:src:F.2.2}
\StatementRecord{maps:src:F.2.2}{proved}{GPT-6 Astra (OpenAI, ChatGPT Pro mode), S6\_06\_BLIND, effort Pro, 2026-11-17; Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic), effort high, 16 November 2026; also checked in this writing by \CurrentChecker}{the hypotheses, notation and definitions stated here; \cref{maps:src:F.1.4}}


The linear order of a finite matrix in $\operatorname{GL}_6(\mathbb Z)$
which admits a free affine lift belongs to
\[
 \{1,2,3,4,5,6,8,10,12\}.
 \tag{F.3}\label{maps:eq:F.3}
\]
There are 38 possible degree-six cyclotomic characteristic
polynomials with an eigenvalue one, and 19 of them commute
with some real complex structure.  These are necessary types,
not 38 or 19 conjugacy classes of admissible tuples.

\end{proposition}

\begin{proposition}[Counterexample: determination by peripheral data alone]\label{maps:src:F.2.3}
\StatementRecord{maps:src:F.2.3}{false as stated; correction proved}{Claude Fable 5.2 (Anthropic), effort high, 16 November 2026; also checked in this writing by \CurrentChecker}{the hypotheses, notation and definitions stated here; the explicit constructions and calculations in the proof}


Monodromy matrices and affine twist vectors alone do not
determine the homology of a compact glued manifold.  A cusp
filling, or an equivalent relative topological specification,
is additional data.

\end{proposition}

